--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Provenance of the fingerprint data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The profile registry records, for each entry, where its bytes were observed
(the `source` prefix of the profile id). No source code from these projects is
copied into or redistributed by this repository -- the entries were produced by
running each tool and recording the bytes it put on the wire, which are
observable facts about a network protocol.

    real:        captured from real browsers on real machines
    linux:       captured from browsers on Linux
    derived:     computed from another entry (documented at the entry)
    utls:        observed from github.com/refraction-networking/utls
                 (via oracle/goutls)
    tls_client:  observed from github.com/bogdanfinn/tls-client
                 (via oracle/gotls, which uses github.com/bogdanfinn/utls)
    curl_cffi:   observed from the curl_cffi Python package
                 (via oracle/utlscollect.py)
    wreq:        observed from the wreq Python package
                 (via oracle/wreqcollect.py)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Build-time dependencies of the verification tools
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Go programs under oracle/ are test oracles written for this project. They
are not part of the library and are not built or shipped with it. They declare
third-party modules in their go.mod files, fetched at build time and governed by
their own licenses:

    github.com/bogdanfinn/tls-client
    github.com/bogdanfinn/utls
    github.com/refraction-networking/utls
    github.com/cloudflare/circl
    github.com/enetx/http, github.com/enetx/http2, github.com/enetx/http3
    github.com/andybalholm/brotli
    golang.org/x/net, golang.org/x/crypto, golang.org/x/sys

The optional Python packages in requirements-dev.txt (curl_cffi, aioquic, wreq)
are likewise fetched at install time and governed by their own licenses.
